From 911bffc0096ebfda932d1c6606daa7c1c2c67c5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:03:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/32] (b) v2, part b-3: float first aid: numbered caption
 after \caption*

The kernel's settings for a replaced \@caption (\fnum@<type> is the
empty label, \ext@<type> is empty, \theH<type> has a unique suffix,
\if@captionstar is true) last until the next \caption. With the float
first aid the next \caption can be float's own, which did not undo them:
a numbered caption after \caption* in the same float lost its label and
its list entry, although the counter was stepped, and its \label got the
target name of the \caption* (with hyperref loaded before float also a
duplicate destination). This happened in restyled floats, \newfloat
types, algorithm.sty, and in plain figures when hyperref is loaded
before float.

float's \caption (without star) now first runs \@caption@nostep@restore
and \@captionstarfalse.

Tests: firstaid-float-caption gets TESTs 5-8 (restyled table, plain
figure, \newfloat, \restylefloat*); new firstaid-float-caption-hyperref
(hyperref loaded before float).

Hook dumps: the .tlg of 15 lthooks and 2 lthooks2 tests show the new code
of package/float/after (only that line changes).
